# Database (Supabase Postgres)

RLS and schema guidance for this chat app.

**Tables:** `chat_room`, `chat_room_member`, `message`, `user_profile`, `realtime.messages`

## Writing RLS Policies

- Output only `CREATE POLICY` or `ALTER POLICY` statements in SQL blocks
- Use `(select auth.uid())` instead of bare `auth.uid()` for performance
- Always specify `TO authenticated` or `TO anon` — never omit roles
- Correct clause order: `ON table FOR operation TO role USING/WITH CHECK`
- Never use `FOR ALL` — create separate SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE policies
- SELECT: `USING` only | INSERT: `WITH CHECK` only | DELETE: `USING` only
- UPDATE: both `USING` and `WITH CHECK`
- Use double quotes for policy names; escape apostrophes in strings (`'Night''s watch'`)
- Prefer **PERMISSIVE** (default) over **RESTRICTIVE** — permissive policies OR together; restrictive AND together and are harder to reason about
- No inline SQL comments in generated policy SQL — put explanations outside the block

## Performance

- Index columns referenced in policies (not already PK/FK indexed)
- Avoid joins in policies — use `IN (SELECT … WHERE user_id = (select auth.uid()))` instead
- `chat_room_member` PK is `(member_id, chat_room_id)` — covers membership lookups
- Add `message(chat_room_id)` index for per-room message queries

## Access Model

| Table | Rule |
| ----- | ---- |
| `user_profile` | All authenticated read; users insert/update own row (`id = auth.uid()`) |
| `chat_room` | Public rooms or member rooms readable; any auth user creates; members update/delete |
| `chat_room_member` | Users see own memberships; self-join public rooms; self-delete to leave |
| `message` | Members read/send in their rooms; `author_id` must equal `auth.uid()` on insert |
| `realtime.messages` | Members SELECT broadcasts on `room:{chat_room_id}:messages` topics |

Room creation via admin/service role bypasses RLS for initial membership insert.

## Reference Policies

```sql
CREATE POLICY "Authenticated users can view all user profiles." ON user_profile
  FOR SELECT TO authenticated
  USING (true);

CREATE POLICY "Users can create their own profile." ON user_profile
  FOR INSERT TO authenticated
  WITH CHECK ((select auth.uid()) = id);

CREATE POLICY "Users can update their own profile." ON user_profile
  FOR UPDATE TO authenticated
  USING ((select auth.uid()) = id)
  WITH CHECK ((select auth.uid()) = id);

CREATE POLICY "Authenticated users can view public rooms or rooms they belong to." ON chat_room
  FOR SELECT TO authenticated
  USING (
    is_public = true
    OR id IN (
      SELECT chat_room_id FROM chat_room_member
      WHERE member_id = (select auth.uid())
    )
  );

CREATE POLICY "Authenticated users can create chat rooms." ON chat_room
  FOR INSERT TO authenticated
  WITH CHECK (true);

CREATE POLICY "Room members can update their chat rooms." ON chat_room
  FOR UPDATE TO authenticated
  USING (
    id IN (
      SELECT chat_room_id FROM chat_room_member
      WHERE member_id = (select auth.uid())
    )
  )
  WITH CHECK (
    id IN (
      SELECT chat_room_id FROM chat_room_member
      WHERE member_id = (select auth.uid())
    )
  );

CREATE POLICY "Room members can delete their chat rooms." ON chat_room
  FOR DELETE TO authenticated
  USING (
    id IN (
      SELECT chat_room_id FROM chat_room_member
      WHERE member_id = (select auth.uid())
    )
  );

CREATE POLICY "Users can view their own room memberships." ON chat_room_member
  FOR SELECT TO authenticated
  USING (member_id = (select auth.uid()));

CREATE POLICY "Users can join public rooms or add themselves as members." ON chat_room_member
  FOR INSERT TO authenticated
  WITH CHECK (
    member_id = (select auth.uid())
    AND (
      EXISTS (
        SELECT 1 FROM chat_room
        WHERE id = chat_room_id AND is_public = true
      )
      OR EXISTS (
        SELECT 1 FROM chat_room_member AS existing
        WHERE existing.chat_room_id = chat_room_id
          AND existing.member_id = (select auth.uid())
      )
    )
  );

CREATE POLICY "Users can leave rooms by removing their own membership." ON chat_room_member
  FOR DELETE TO authenticated
  USING (member_id = (select auth.uid()));

CREATE POLICY "Room members can view messages in their rooms." ON message
  FOR SELECT TO authenticated
  USING (
    chat_room_id IN (
      SELECT chat_room_id FROM chat_room_member
      WHERE member_id = (select auth.uid())
    )
  );

CREATE POLICY "Room members can send messages as themselves." ON message
  FOR INSERT TO authenticated
  WITH CHECK (
    author_id = (select auth.uid())
    AND chat_room_id IN (
      SELECT chat_room_id FROM chat_room_member
      WHERE member_id = (select auth.uid())
    )
  );

CREATE POLICY "Room members can receive message broadcasts for their rooms." ON realtime.messages
  FOR SELECT TO authenticated
  USING (
    topic LIKE 'room:%:messages'
    AND EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM chat_room_member
      WHERE member_id = (select auth.uid())
        AND chat_room_id = SPLIT_PART(topic, ':', 2)::uuid
    )
  );
```

## Migrations

- Use `apply_migration` for DDL (policies, triggers, indexes)
- Store local migrations in `supabase/migrations/`
- Regenerate types after schema changes: `npm run gen-types`
